  "correct": "C",
  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Expose the hidden quadratic",
      "body": "<p>Set <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>cos</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></mrow></math>, with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>. The equation becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>.</p>",
      "recap": "The range restriction is as important as the factorisation.",
      "pitfall": "The substituted variable is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>cos</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></mrow></math>, not <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></mrow></math>.",
      "pause": "Factor the quadratic.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b3-l04",
          "reminder": "A polynomial in a repeated expression can be simplified by a substitution with a known range."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Filter the possible cosine squares",
      "body": "<p>Solve the quadratic and compare each root with the range of the substituted variable. For every permitted square value, recover every possible cosine sign.</p>",
      "recap": "Squaring combines sign branches; recovering them requires checking both signs.",
      "pitfall": "A real quadratic root need not be a possible squared cosine.",
      "pause": "Derive the permitted cosine values before listing angles.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l16",
          "reminder": "Squaring combines sign branches; recovering them requires checking both signs."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Count the inclusive endpoints",
      "body": "<p>Use the cosine graph to find every input for each permitted cosine value. Check both ends of the stated closed interval separately.</p>",
      "recap": "Count distinct input angles, including allowed endpoints.",
      "pitfall": "One full cycle can include both endpoints when the interval is closed.",
      "pause": "List the allowed angles and count them once each.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b2-l04",
          "reminder": "Trig solution counts depend on branches and whether the interval endpoints are included."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "solution": "<p>With <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x02208;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow></math>, the equation factors as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>. The root <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math> is impossible, so <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>cos</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>&#x000B1;</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p>In <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#x003C0;</mi></mrow></math>, the solutions are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mtext>&#x000A0;</mtext><mi>&#x003C0;</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mtext>&#x000A0;</mtext><mn>2</mn><mi>&#x003C0;</mi></mrow></math>. Both endpoints are included and are distinct values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>Answer C: 3 solutions.</strong></p>",
